Package: lcos-branding
Version: 1.1.0-1
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: 12268
Maintainer: LCOS <lcos@lunduke.com>
Homepage: https://lunduke.com
Depends: plymouth-label
Provides: lcos-branding
Replaces: lcos-branding (<< 0.7)
Conflicts: lcos-branding (<< 0.7)
Description: LCOS 1.1.0 artwork (wallpapers, splash, logos, Plymouth)
 LCOS 1.1.0 artwork: stock wallpaper (jpg), synthwave nebula-grid, 4K wood
 backdrop, GRUB splash (default / 1024x768 / 4K), logos, and the LCOS
 Plymouth boot theme (frames + Shutdown-1.png) plus the LightDM
 greeter/session setup helper (lcos-display-fix: .Xauthority seeding;
 no longer quits Plymouth, LightDM does). postinst sets Theme=lcos when
 plymouth is present.
 Replaces old lcos-branding 1.0-2 / 0.2.0 (bw-720 + lcos32 only).
 .
 0.9.6-1: drops the duplicate lcos-desktop-stock.png (same 1792x1008
 picture as lcos-desktop-stock.jpg; nothing referenced it) from
 /usr/share/backgrounds/lcos, /usr/share/xfce4/backdrops and
 /usr/share/images/desktop-base. lcos-desktop-stock.jpg stays the stock
 wallpaper. Editor 2026-10-23.
 1.0.1-2: the Plymouth script theme draws the passphrase prompt over
 the splash (#196). Depends plymouth-label (label-pango.so; script
 themes cannot draw text without it, and update-initramfs warns when
 it is missing). On upgrade from below 1.0.1-2, postinst runs
 update-initramfs so an installed encrypted system picks up the theme
 and the label plugin. Editor 2026-11-07.
 1.0.1-3: that upgrade rebuild uses "update-initramfs -u -k all", so
 every installed kernel gets the label plugin, not only the newest.
 1.0.1-2 left initrd.img-7.2.6-lunduke without label-pango.so, and an
 encrypted 1.0 system that boots 7.2.6 from Advanced options missed the
 LUKS prompt text. The one-shot runs on upgrade from below 1.0.1-3.
 Editor 2026-11-08.
 1.1.0-1: version bump for LCOS 1.1.0. No functional changes.
 Editor 2026-11-12.
